{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016JHUoURwiRmvXpBeCFgKhr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context and propose tasks for release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum).\n\nLooking at the constraints:\n- Max 1 task\n- Release scope: only 05.4\n- 150-250 lines production code per task\n- Max 4 PRD sub-requirements per task\n\nI need to find the PRD for the checksum utilities. The project context mentions rel05.4 with use cases for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum. All have specstatus: spec_complete, codestatus: not started.\n\n\nSince I can't access the files directly, I'm working from the context provided. The checksum utilities follow a consistent pattern—they all read files or stdin, compute the hash, and output in standard format, so they likely share a common PRD. I notice there's a previous task in the git history that implemented these binaries on the generation branch, but the code status still shows \"not started\" in the current analysis, which suggests I need to check what's actually on the current branch.\n\nGiven the 250-line limit and the fact that these four utilities are nearly identical except for their hash algorithms, I should propose combining them into a single task. Each one essentially does the same thing: read input, compute the hash, print the result in \"hash  filename\" format, and support a --check mode for verification. The main variation is just which hash algorithm gets used. Since the cmd/ files would be thin wrappers selecting the algorithm, and there's no shared checksum package in the architecture, I'll propose one task that covers all four binaries together.\n\nI'm not certain about the exact PRD numbers for each checksum utility, but the recent commit references them as separate PRDs for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, and sha512sum. I should reference them by their expected file paths based on the project's naming convention. , the checksum PRDs are likely higher numbers. I'll need to reference them by name pattern.\n\nGiven I can only propose 1 task, let me make it count. The checksum utilities are trivially similar - each one reads files or stdin, computes a specific hash, outputs in GNU coreutils format, supports --check mode for verification, handles binary/text flags, and manages SIGPIPE. All four can share the same implementation pattern, so I'll propose implementing all four cmd/ binaries at once.\n\nFor the PRD paths, I don't have exact numbers for the checksum specs, but I can reference them by glob pattern or use case IDs. I'll just propose the task with reasonable assumptions about where they're located and let the stitch agent read them directly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27584,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27584},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c4a5e5d-040b-4197-a25f-ccebb70308bc","uuid":"106a3a71-1e18-4d01-b96e-762104e8a12c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016JHUoURwiRmvXpBeCFgKhr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator) by regenerating GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go from formal specs, verified via differential testing against Homebrew GNU binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs/use cases; orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` using `pkg/` shared libraries (sys, format, testutils). Differential testing in `pkg/testutils` gates all code.\n\n**Current state:** Specs exist for releases 00.0 through 05.4 plus 99.2. All have codestatus \"not started\" in this generation branch. Release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) is the target.\n\n**Current release:** 05.4 — four use cases, all spec_complete, none implemented.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 05.4 contains four nearly identical utilities differing only in hash algorithm. All four share the same flag set (--check, --binary, --text, --status, --warn, --strict, --quiet) and the same output format (`hash  filename`). They can be implemented in a single task within the 250-line budget since each `main.go` is ~40-50 lines with a shared pattern, and Go's `crypto/*` packages handle the algorithm differences.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement checksum quartet cmd/ binaries (prd md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (all prd*md5sum*, prd*sha1sum*, prd*sha256sum*, prd*sha512sum* files)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section for differential testing and SIGPIPE patterns)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests signature)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference for cmd/ structure and differential test pattern)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference for test file structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: md5sum binary using crypto/md5\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gmd5sum\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha1sum binary using crypto/sha1\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha1sum\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha256sum binary using crypto/sha256\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha256sum\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum binary using crypto/sha512\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha512sum\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement cmd/md5sum, cmd/sha1sum, cmd/sha256sum, and cmd/sha512sum as standalone binaries.\n          Each binary reads files listed on the command line (or stdin if no files given) and prints\n          the checksum and filename in GNU coreutils format: \"<hash>  <filename>\\n\" (two spaces for\n          text mode, space-asterisk for binary mode). Use crypto/md5, crypto/sha1, crypto/sha256,\n          and crypto/sha512 respectively from Go's standard library.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Support --check (-c) mode: read lines in the format \"<hash>  <filename>\" or\n          \"<hash> *<filename>\", recompute the hash for each file, and report OK or FAILED.\n          Exit 0 if all checks pass, exit 1 if any check fails. Support --status (suppress output,\n          exit code only), --warn (-w, warn about improperly formatted lines), --strict (exit\n          non-zero for improperly formatted lines), and --quiet (suppress OK lines in check output).\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Support --binary (-b) and --text (-t) flags. On GNU/POSIX systems these are equivalent\n          (no CR/LF translation), but --binary changes the output format to use \" *\" instead of\n          \"  \" between hash and filename. Default is text mode. When reading from stdin with no\n          filename args, use \"-\" as the filename in output.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for each utility. Use testutils.BuildBinary to compile the Go\n          binary and exec.LookPath to find the GNU reference binary (gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum,\n          gsha512sum). Call t.Skip if the reference binary is not found. Use testutils.RunDiffTests\n          to compare stdout, stderr, and exit code. Test cases must cover: single file, multiple\n          files, stdin, --check mode with valid and invalid checksums, --binary flag output format,\n          missing file error, and --quiet/--status/--warn/--strict flag interactions with --check.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() in each binary, per the\n          shared SIGPIPE protocol in ARCHITECTURE.yaml.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Each cmd/<utility>/main.go is a self-contained binary. Do NOT create a shared checksum\n          package in pkg/. The four binaries are small enough that minor duplication of flag parsing\n          is acceptable and keeps each utility independent. If the main logic (hash-and-print,\n          check-mode) exceeds 30 lines, extract it into unexported functions within the same package.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") to build the Go binary under test. Reference binary\n          names follow the Homebrew g-prefix convention: gmd5sum, gsha1sum, gsha256sum, gsha512sum.\n          If exec.LookPath fails for the reference binary, call t.Skipf -- do NOT attempt to\n          install any packages.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          For --check mode parsing, accept both \"<hash>  <filename>\" (text mode, two spaces) and\n          \"<hash> *<filename>\" (binary mode, space-asterisk). Lines that do not match either format\n          are improperly formatted -- warn or error depending on --warn/--strict flags.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/md5sum/main.go, cmd/sha1sum/main.go, cmd/sha256sum/main.go, cmd/sha512sum/main.go each compile to a standalone binary with go build.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Each binary produces GNU-compatible output format: '<hex-hash>  <filename>' for text mode, '<hex-hash> *<filename>' for binary mode.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Each binary's --check mode correctly verifies checksums and exits 0 on all-pass, 1 on any failure.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Differential tests exist in each cmd/<utility>/<utility>_test.go and pass when the GNU reference binary is available.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"All four binaries handle stdin input (no filename args) and print '-' as the filename.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/md5sum/... ./cmd/sha1sum/... ./cmd/sha256sum/... ./cmd/sha512sum/... reports no errors.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27584,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27584},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c4a5e5d-040b-4197-a25f-ccebb70308bc","uuid":"75b96041-eef7-48b2-9d78-d72eea9c8cc2"}
